From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:33:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] AROS: no volume requesters

FGData names files as "/Aircraft/...", and such a path is tried as
written before it is looked for under FG_ROOT. With Unix path syntax on
AROS that is the volume "Aircraft:", and DOS asks for it to be inserted.
main() turns the requesters off for the process (fgaros_no_requesters()
of the port's libfgaros); threads inherit that.
---
 src/Main/bootstrap.cxx | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Main/bootstrap.cxx b/src/Main/bootstrap.cxx
index ab20ae2..a8670bb 100755
--- a/src/Main/bootstrap.cxx
+++ b/src/Main/bootstrap.cxx
@@ -274,8 +274,15 @@ bool detectSIMD() { return true; }
 int _bootstrap_OSInit;
 
 // Main entry point; catch any exceptions that have made it this far.
+#if defined(__AROS__)
+extern "C" void fgaros_no_requesters(void);
+#endif
+
 int main ( int argc, char **argv )
 {
+#if defined(__AROS__)
+    fgaros_no_requesters();
+#endif
     // we don't want to accidently show a GUI box and block startup in
     // non_GUI setups, so check this value early here, before options are
     // processed
